1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,994
This video uses offline macOS system-generated narration with the Aman voice.

2
00:00:03,994 --> 00:00:07,323
I am presenting a bounded ad safety decision-support prototype.

3
00:00:07,323 --> 00:00:12,981
I turn one ad image into an APPROVE, REVIEW, or BLOCK recommendation while keeping the evidence visible.

4
00:00:12,981 --> 00:00:18,640
The formal result is strong, but I do not treat this pilot as approval for autonomous deployment.

5
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:21,592
I divide the story across four presenters.

6
00:00:21,592 --> 00:00:24,123
Swarnaditya covers the decision and results.

7
00:00:24,123 --> 00:00:26,654
Vijay covers data and failure analysis.

8
00:00:26,654 --> 00:00:29,184
Myetchae covers policy, architecture, and audit.

9
00:00:29,184 --> 00:00:31,715
Bickramjit covers method, literature, and workflow.

10
00:00:31,715 --> 00:00:33,917
I start from a queue problem.

11
00:00:33,917 --> 00:00:39,788
A creative can hide a restricted object, subtle text, or misleading context inside an ordinary image.

12
00:00:39,788 --> 00:00:41,990
Manual review is slow and inconsistent.

13
00:00:41,990 --> 00:00:49,329
I therefore use computer vision to prioritize risky images and show evidence, while a person remains the final decision maker.

14
00:00:49,329 --> 00:00:54,603
My modeled boundary has four image labels: safe, firearms, explosives, and financial promotion.

15
00:00:54,603 --> 00:01:01,905
Financial content always routes to REVIEW because an image cannot prove a misleading claim or a legal violation.

16
00:01:01,905 --> 00:01:08,801
The prototype does not model explicit content, violence, alcohol, tobacco, geography, age restrictions, landing pages, advertiser identity,

17
00:01:08,801 --> 00:01:10,829
or the full policy rulebook.

18
00:01:10,829 --> 00:01:13,472
I built a 288-image pilot dataset.

19
00:01:13,472 --> 00:01:18,758
Each class has 48 training images, 12 validation images, and 12 untouched test images.

20
00:01:18,758 --> 00:01:25,177
I split 215 source groups so the same campaign or exact source group stays in one partition.

21
00:01:25,177 --> 00:01:30,463
This blocks a simple duplicate leak, but balanced counts do not remove source bias.

22
00:01:30,463 --> 00:01:33,031
The contact sheet exposes the main weakness.

23
00:01:33,031 --> 00:01:35,232
Safe ads are synthetic product creatives.

24
00:01:35,232 --> 00:01:37,066
Financial ads are synthetic templates.

25
00:01:37,066 --> 00:01:40,001
Both weapon classes come from one weapons source.

26
00:01:40,001 --> 00:01:44,036
A classifier can therefore learn photographic style instead of policy meaning.

27
00:01:44,036 --> 00:01:48,805
I call this source confounding, and it limits every formal score that follows.

28
00:01:48,805 --> 00:01:51,420
My pipeline keeps three evidence streams separate.

29
00:01:51,420 --> 00:01:54,408
A frozen vision transformer scores the whole image.

30
00:01:54,408 --> 00:01:57,397
Grounding DINO can localize weapon and explosive cues.

31
00:01:57,397 --> 00:01:58,891
Tesseract extracts visible words.

32
00:01:58,891 --> 00:02:04,867
A versioned policy layer then combines classifier, detector, and text evidence into APPROVE, REVIEW, or BLOCK.

33
00:02:04,867 --> 00:02:10,470
This design makes each reason inspectable instead of hiding the final action inside one score.

34
00:02:10,470 --> 00:02:17,635
I froze both the V-I-T and ResNet-fifty backbones, cached their embeddings, and fit logistic heads only on training data.

35
00:02:17,635 --> 00:02:20,240
I selected conservative class thresholds on validation data.

36
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:23,822
I opened the 48-image test set once for final reporting.

37
00:02:23,822 --> 00:02:30,010
I also benchmarked warm batch-one C-P-U inference with one thread so the timing protocol stays reproducible.

38
00:02:30,010 --> 00:02:35,806
I use published work to justify component choices, not to claim this pilot is production-ready.

39
00:02:35,806 --> 00:02:39,067
The V-I-T paper supports transferable image representations.

40
00:02:39,067 --> 00:02:41,603
Grounding DINO supports text-conditioned object localization.

41
00:02:41,603 --> 00:02:43,414
Tesseract supports visible-text extraction.

42
00:02:43,414 --> 00:02:47,399
Only this project's saved evaluation supports the numbers I report.

43
00:02:47,399 --> 00:02:55,904
On the untouched 48-image test, my V-I-T reached macro F one of 0.97913 and accuracy of 0.97917.

44
00:02:55,904 --> 00:03:00,543
The frozen ResNet-fifty baseline reached macro F one of 0.87315.

45
00:03:00,543 --> 00:03:07,116
Safe precision 1.0 means the proposal's greater-than-0.98 Safe-class precision benchmark passed.

46
00:03:07,116 --> 00:03:12,528
The Safe-ad false-flag rate, defined as one minus Safe recall, was zero.

47
00:03:12,528 --> 00:03:20,260
Multiclass argmax restricted-class mean recall 0.97222 differs from the threshold-operating mean 0.94444 and minimum 0.91667.

48
00:03:20,260 --> 00:03:26,059
The proposal's per-class greater-than-0.95 target failed for firearms and explosives.

49
00:03:26,059 --> 00:03:32,632
The 0.90 validation-recall tuning floor in code was only for calibration, not that acceptance target.

50
00:03:32,632 --> 00:03:41,523
Warm C-P-U batch-one P ninety-five latency was 71.527 milliseconds for V-I-T and 40.064 for ResNet.

51
00:03:41,523 --> 00:03:45,776
The V-I-T classifier path exceeded the 50-millisecond target.

52
00:03:45,776 --> 00:03:52,348
Full end-to-end P ninety-five remains unassessed because this timing covers preprocessing and classification only.

53
00:03:52,348 --> 00:03:57,761
It excludes file decoding, O-C-R, object detection, network transfer, and app rendering.

54
00:03:57,761 --> 00:03:59,929
The test had one classification error.

55
00:03:59,929 --> 00:04:04,990
An explosives image was predicted as firearms, so 47 of 48 labels were correct.

56
00:04:04,990 --> 00:04:09,688
In the saved demo, the fused policy score for firearms is 0.88998.

57
00:04:09,688 --> 00:04:15,110
Neither the calibrated firearms threshold nor the explosives threshold fires, so the policy returns REVIEW.

58
00:04:15,110 --> 00:04:18,363
The detector still localizes shotgun and grenade-like cues.

59
00:04:18,363 --> 00:04:21,616
This is a class mistake, not an automatic approval.

60
00:04:21,616 --> 00:04:25,333
I then tested a manually reviewed 26-image Wikimedia diagnostic set.

61
00:04:25,333 --> 00:04:31,754
Classifier macro F one fell to 0.55489, and the detector's nonweapon false-positive rate reached 0.90.

62
00:04:31,754 --> 00:04:34,119
This historical shoe ad is labeled safe.

63
00:04:34,119 --> 00:04:41,553
The classifier predicts explosives at 0.32411, detector evidence raises the fused policy score to 0.45302, and the policy returns BLOCK.

64
00:04:41,553 --> 00:04:44,595
The detector boxes and heatmap concentrate on the shoe.

65
00:04:44,595 --> 00:04:47,974
This is direct evidence of domain shift and source confounding.

66
00:04:47,974 --> 00:04:51,691
The small diagnostic sample is not a second formal test set.

67
00:04:51,691 --> 00:04:53,274
The workspace has four steps.

68
00:04:53,274 --> 00:05:00,238
I upload one J-P-E-G, P-N-G, or WebP image, configure optional object context, O-C-R, and occlusion,

69
00:05:00,238 --> 00:05:05,303
review raw and fused scores with reasons and timing, then export a case-level audit record.

70
00:05:05,303 --> 00:05:07,519
The policy returns APPROVE, REVIEW, or BLOCK.

71
00:05:07,519 --> 00:05:09,735
I use four saved formal examples next.

72
00:05:09,735 --> 00:05:13,624
For the safe formal example, the classifier score is 0.99735.

73
00:05:13,624 --> 00:05:19,282
O-C-R finds three tokens, the optional detector is off, and the policy returns APPROVE.

74
00:05:19,282 --> 00:05:23,525
I can trace the verdict to the saved input and audit record.

75
00:05:23,525 --> 00:05:28,475
This confirms the intended path for an ordinary product creative inside the pilot domain.

76
00:05:28,475 --> 00:05:33,006
For the firearm example, the fused policy score is 0.99907.

77
00:05:33,006 --> 00:05:39,596
Grounding DINO returns three detections, the evidence overlay localizes weapon cues, and the policy returns BLOCK.

78
00:05:39,596 --> 00:05:48,245
The optional detector and heatmap take seconds, so their latency must not be confused with the 71.527-millisecond classifier benchmark.

79
00:05:48,245 --> 00:05:54,127
For the explosives example, the fused policy score is 0.99981 and the detector returns three boxes.

80
00:05:54,127 --> 00:05:58,279
The overlay identifies grenade and bomb-like cues among the surrounding objects.

81
00:05:58,279 --> 00:05:59,663
The policy returns BLOCK.

82
00:05:59,663 --> 00:06:07,275
This is the clean in-domain success case, and it contrasts with the earlier grenade image that crossed into the firearms class.

83
00:06:07,275 --> 00:06:14,001
For the financial promotion example, the classifier score is 0.99921 and O-C-R extracts 17 tokens.

84
00:06:14,001 --> 00:06:16,617
The policy still returns REVIEW, not BLOCK,

85
00:06:16,617 --> 00:06:22,595
because this prototype cannot determine whether a financial claim is lawful or misleading from pixels alone.

86
00:06:22,595 --> 00:06:28,201
The text and heatmap give a reviewer useful context without replacing legal or policy judgment.

87
00:06:28,201 --> 00:06:34,856
The largest risks are source-confounded training data, an uncalibrated detector outside the pilot domain, and incomplete policy coverage.

88
00:06:34,856 --> 00:06:37,308
The formal test has only 48 images.

89
00:06:37,308 --> 00:06:39,410
The external audit has only 26.

90
00:06:39,410 --> 00:06:43,263
Full end-to-end latency and concurrent throughput were not measured.

91
00:06:43,263 --> 00:06:49,568
M-P-S resource use was not measured, including C-P-U, G-P-U, and memory use.

92
00:06:49,568 --> 00:06:57,274
Before an M-V-P trial, I need diverse real ads, local detector calibration, out-of-distribution checks, audit logs, human escalation,

93
00:06:57,274 --> 00:06:59,726
and monitoring for drift and subgroup failures.

94
00:06:59,726 --> 00:07:03,864
My recommendation is only a human-gated M-V-P, not autonomous enforcement.

95
00:07:03,864 --> 00:07:08,002
The recommended ten-week roadmap is a planning assumption, not a measured commitment.

96
00:07:08,002 --> 00:07:14,369
In weeks one through three, a data lead, policy reviewer, and two annotators build a campaign-grouped real-ad holdout.

97
00:07:14,369 --> 00:07:20,736
In weeks four through six, one M-L engineer and a reviewer recalibrate the system against the declared quality gates.

98
00:07:20,736 --> 00:07:25,511
In weeks seven through ten, product, M-L-Ops, and reviewers run a shadow pilot.

99
00:07:25,511 --> 00:07:34,106
The scale gate tests ten concurrent requests and measures end-to-end p ninety-five plus C-P-U, G-P-U, and memory before broader rollout.

